Article 3 (Composition)
(1) The Committee shall consist of not more than 15 members, including one Chairperson, and one member other than the Chairperson shall serve as a standing member. <Amended on September 6, 2016.>
(2) Members shall be commissioned by the Minister of the National Court Administration from among persons falling under any of the following:
1. Judges;
2. Attorneys-at-law;
3. University professors;
4. Public officials of administrative agencies;
5. Financial experts with experience working at financial institutions;
6. Other persons with knowledge and experience.
(3) The Chairperson and standing member shall be designated by the Minister of the National Court Administration from among the members. <Amended on September 6, 2016.>
(4) The term of office of members shall be two years, and members may be reappointed.
(5) The Minister of the National Court Administration may dismiss a member from his or her commission in any of the following cases:
1. Where the member is deemed unable to perform duties due to unavoidable circumstances;
2. Where the member violates duties in the performance of his or her office;
3. Where the member is otherwise deemed unfit to continue to qualify as a member.
